      "worked": "The median is the mean of the third and fourth values. The missing value must lie between $9$ and $14$, giving middle values $x$ and $14$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x+14}{2}&=12\\\\x+14&=24\\\\x&=10\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: the ordered cards are $7,\\ 9,\\ 10,\\ 14,\\ 20,\\ 30$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{Median}&=\\frac{10+14}{2}\\\\\\mathrm{Median}&=12\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
